{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more","id":1476953,"title":"Should the S.I. fight werewolves more?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-22T06:45:34-07:00","id":1476953,"title":"Should the S.I. fight werewolves more?","content":"I mean, from the S.I. perspective, werewolves are terrorists who routinely attack mundane corporations. One would think they'd be a higher priority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T06:48:42-07:00","id":1476954,"title":"","content":"I suspect the out of universe reason is that the writers want werewolves to have their own human organisation against them. Be it Pentex or something else<br /> The in universe might be that Delirium works on si agents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T06:59:47-07:00","id":1476956,"title":"","content":"The original werewolves were pretty much unkillable by conventional human means (and quite a few supernatural ones), I guess the SI is probably not that powerful enough that they can afford to arm an entire infantry division with silver bullets and send them to get slaughtered only to kill a couple of garous, that is if they don't end up nerfing the woofs too (which seems likely at this point), in that case I would expect Pentex to back the SI in some ways as to go after garous too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T07:07:06-07:00","id":1476957,"title":"","content":"Possibly. But the Garou usually also tend to do things to keep the Veil. Their primary goal of the Garou is to fight the wyrm, not necessarily to strike terror into the humans. And possibly there might be Fomori corpses and other stuff that mundane first responders should not find, so the garou might be better in hiding their presence then for example anarch neonates....<br /> <br /> Government agencies have always be a low key problem for garou though... and I don't think that needs to change. I mean, it should be addressed that the second inquisition exists, but not be stylised into a prime-antagonist or anything like that...<br /> <br /> Hey, were the Hunter: The Reckoning Play Station games ever canon? For there are hordes and hordes of zombies around. Why did that never turn up on the Second Inquisitions radar?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T07:11:08-07:00","id":1476958,"title":"","content":"Is there a 2nd Inquisition tie to Strike Force Zero from Demon Hunter X. For they sure could lend a lot of tactical and technological help.....<br /> <br /> Just imagine an western intelligence agency director telling his Japanese counterpart in a secret meeting that there are supernatural beings influencing the world and that they are now setting up a Task Force to eradicate them and he just goes like &quot;Sure, we've done that fifteen years ago.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T11:51:58-07:00","id":1476994,"title":"","content":"I won't comment on the Second Inquisition per se because I don't like V5, but I am a big believer in having a more active and successful hunter organizations than what was previously portrayed in the earlier settings. The original Society of Leopold and handful of other organizations were fine when 1e vampire material was put out, but they were quickly overclassed as 2e vampire developed and Revised inflated things even more. It became harder to think hunters provided any real threat to vampires.<br /> <br /> Now in terms of Werewolf, the game always downplayed the threat of hunters to the Garou. Mentions of the Society of Leopold basically said they didn't hunt werewolves outside exceptional circumstances. The only explicit Werewolf hunting organization was DNA, and even they were turned into a Weaver influenced organization that raised issues of the Triat, rather than a group of werewolf hunters who had access to high tech weapons in order to counter balance the game mechanics of the Garou. (The DNA described in Book of the Weaver is very different from its original description in the corebooks.) So werewolf hunters are a neglected aspect of the setting. I think the setting would be improved by having real, credible werewolf hunters in them provided it fit Gothic Horror genre and the game's conventions.<br /> <br /> I've started a few threads on that subject in this forum, and gained some good ideas from it. But I'm still working on getting those ideas into a good format for my own chronicles. I have figured out how I wanted to portray the Society of Leopold in their views on werewolves and when they'd become involved. Still working on an actual separate, secular group of werewolf hunters; I have the basic concept worked out but still working on the details. And in modern era chronicles, I returned DNA to being just a group of werewolf hunters hoping to use Garou specimens to learn medical secrets that can help people (and therefore PROFIT!), rather than the more supernatural Weaver group that is trying to &quot;cure&quot; Garou for no financial benefit at all (and whose actions would cause the company to lose money, not gain it).<br /> <br /> Having said this, I've learned that as much as I love hunters in the setting, that I've never successfully used them in an actual game. Players hate it when the ST tries to kill their characters (even if it is only done when they do things that threaten the Masquerade/Veil and thus is &quot;fair&quot; consequences of their actions), and deeply resent the ST making hunters smart and effective when they try to hunt (since smart hunters would fight to their strengths, not those of the enemy). But the alternative - making them stupid and easily killable to assuage players' feelings - just makes hunters useless and undermines the genre. So I use them more as background element that affects NPCs, not players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T13:29:11-07:00","id":1477007,"title":"","content":"It is a little strange, since most werewolf fiction has them dying to quite mundane hunters. The Howling werewolves get slaughtered by a reporter with a rifle. The American werewolf in London dies to police. The original 30's werewolf dies to a guy with a silver cane. This idea that you need Captain Planet villains to give werewolves a rough fight seems to be entirely the creation of White Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T18:56:45-07:00","id":1477048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1476956#post1476956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original werewolves were pretty much unkillable by conventional human means (and quite a few supernatural ones), I guess the SI is probably not that powerful enough that they can afford to arm an entire infantry division with silver bullets and send them to get slaughtered only to kill a couple of garous, that is if they don't end up nerfing the woofs too (which seems likely at this point), in that case I would expect Pentex to back the SI in some ways as to go after garous too.</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually super are that powerful. The book has stats for a whole lot of really cool toys, but does offer that they have ac-130s at their disposal. No crinos is going to survive that. <br /> <br /> I think it\u2019s more that the SI targets \u201cblank bodies\u201d as a direct threat against humanity, where as the garou, if you know about them, tend to try to not do that. Lower on the radar. Particularly with the sabbat doing the Gehenna war and drawing all that attention to themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T19:37:32-07:00","id":1477050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477048#post1477048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They actually super are that powerful. The book has stats for a whole lot of really cool toys, but does offer that they have ac-130s at their disposal. No crinos is going to survive that.<br /> <br /> I think it\u2019s more that the SI targets \u201cblank bodies\u201d as a direct threat against humanity, where as the garou, if you know about them, tend to try to not do that. Lower on the radar. Particularly with the sabbat doing the Gehenna war and drawing all that attention to themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be honest, I think that werewolves would be a priority target for the SI, unlike vamps who operate largely under the radar and aren't that big on bodycount, werewolves regularly engage in acts of terrorism, leave corpses wherever they go and are generally not that subtle compared to vamps.<br /> <br /> I haven't red the SI book but if they get to use that kind of military hardware then they would definitely be more than capable of dealing with garous, granted carpet bombing natural reserves is going to raise questions but I guess that they would be able to cover it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T21:00:48-07:00","id":1477052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477007#post1477007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a little strange, since most werewolf fiction has them dying to quite mundane hunters. The Howling werewolves get slaughtered by a reporter with a rifle. The American werewolf in London dies to police. The original 30's werewolf dies to a guy with a silver cane. This idea that you need Captain Planet villains to give werewolves a rough fight seems to be entirely the creation of White Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's an artifact of it being a roleplaying game. Not some conscious decision by White Wolf as a setting element. You want your vampire, werewolf, whatever PC to be tough and powerful so the game is fun, and that makes sense since you're a supernatural creature. At the same time, the horror genre - since its protagonists are usually ordinary people and not the monsters - give us lots of examples of ordinary people slaying the monsters because they are the heroes.<br /> <br /> So in Dracula you can have a psychologist, a physician, a lawyer, a secretary, an aristocrat, and a cowboy kill the lord of the vampires. But if it happened to a VtM PC, the player would get upset because he'd argue his supernatural powers should make him be able to destroy a small group of mortals easily. So the game has traditionally downplayed how effective hunters can be. in Werewolf, the Garou are supposed to be even more combat worthy so the hunters are even more ineffectual. (Not to mention in horror media, it's usually the mortal protagonists that organize in groups and fight monsters that are alone, or defeat them one by one if they do happen to be in groups. In RPGs, the PCs are usually together as a group.)<br /> <br /> At the same time, silver is supposed to provide unsoakable aggravated damage, so it always seemed to me that informed mortals should be a lot more dangerous to werewolves than vampires. It all depends on how effective the Veil or Masquerade is.<br /> <br /> In chronicles I run, if I want to emphasize the danger of mortal hunters, I do it by background elements like NPCs talking at the sept at how some lone Ronin or Lost Cub got killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T22:01:43-07:00","id":1477168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477050#post1477050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I think that werewolves would be a priority target for the SI, unlike vamps who operate largely under the radar and aren't that big on bodycount, werewolves regularly engage in acts of terrorism, leave corpses wherever they go and are generally not that subtle compared to vamps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much.<br /> <br /> There are two big differences that <i>could</i> justify the SI not targeting Garou so much.<br /> <br /> 1 - Gehenna War. The Sabbat is currently in canon the main responsible for making Vampires high profile. Other supernaturals rarely have a group so dedicated to drawing attention to themselves. In fact, despite their reputation, even the old Sabbat had a far lower profile than the new Sabbat. That matters a lot.<br /> <br /> 2 - High profile operations. Vampires are mostly urbane. They wander the cities preying on humans. They infiltrate big organizations. They lend their cursed powers to ghouls. In other words, while they're usually subtle, they're simply everywhere, especially from the PoV of people especially paranoid about government infiltration.<br /> <br /> Werewolves barely live near humans. Most are in rural or wild areas, ad even when they're in cities they're frequently in the city's Umbra. They may not be subtle in their interactions, but Garou interaction with humanity is quite rarer than what Vampires do. Kinfolk do not have any special power at all, and they not so much infiltrate anything as they simply <b>are</b> members of normal society, just with Garou ties. All together, stepping sideways and shape-changing are enough to make the few signs of werewolf activity pretty hard to piece together without a lot of inside knowledge of their ways and abilities.<br /> <br /> Doubly so when the places they raze are already frequently messed up to a point where to onlookers after the fact it could very well be just an accident, and the Wyrm servants themselves working to cover up what really happened because they may also be found out in the process (and, well, they <b>are</b> a cabal of cannibalistic child molesters and all that). Add in Delirium and magical resources to cleanse scenes from evidence, and I don't see a reason for the SI to be more wary from the Garou than Vampires unless the plot needs it to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T02:39:41-07:00","id":1477183,"title":"","content":"You know who should the S.I focus on? Kinfolk and Skin Dancers. Remember, your average Society of Leopold grunt doesn't know much more about werewolves than what is in folklore and in movies. So they should be looking at things like werewolf pelts, werewolf related rituals,etc. Some kinfolk have the feral appearance merit as well.<br /> <br /> Essentially, they'd not be hunting the 9-foot furry blenders, but those who seem to show signs of 'contract with the devil' with looking feral or scrounging up werewolf/wolf pelts.<br /> <br /> This way, the S.I can easily affect the garou without ever being just a bother in the battlefield.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T03:55:26-07:00","id":1477187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477168#post1477168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much.<br /> <br /> There are two big differences that <i>could</i> justify the SI not targeting Garou so much.<br /> <br /> 1 - Gehenna War. The Sabbat is currently in canon the main responsible for making Vampires high profile. Other supernaturals rarely have a group so dedicated to drawing attention to themselves. In fact, despite their reputation, even the old Sabbat had a far lower profile than the new Sabbat. That matters a lot.<br /> <br /> 2 - High profile operations. Vampires are mostly urbane. They wander the cities preying on humans. They infiltrate big organizations. They lend their cursed powers to ghouls. In other words, while they're usually subtle, they're simply everywhere, especially from the PoV of people especially paranoid about government infiltration.<br /> <br /> Werewolves barely live near humans. Most are in rural or wild areas, ad even when they're in cities they're frequently in the city's Umbra. They may not be subtle in their interactions, but Garou interaction with humanity is quite rarer than what Vampires do. Kinfolk do not have any special power at all, and they not so much infiltrate anything as they simply <b>are</b> members of normal society, just with Garou ties. All together, stepping sideways and shape-changing are enough to make the few signs of werewolf activity pretty hard to piece together without a lot of inside knowledge of their ways and abilities.<br /> <br /> Doubly so when the places they raze are already frequently messed up to a point where to onlookers after the fact it could very well be just an accident, and the Wyrm servants themselves working to cover up what really happened because they may also be found out in the process (and, well, they <b>are</b> a cabal of cannibalistic child molesters and all that). Add in Delirium and magical resources to cleanse scenes from evidence, and I don't see a reason for the SI to be more wary from the Garou than Vampires unless the plot needs it to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did you play werewolf heart of the forest? Granted its a multiple choice game but most garou operations end in a similar bloodbath, delirium and all can only do so much when you butcher a small town, compared to what werewolves usually do, the sabbat is almost a joke even in the current iteration where they suddenly turned into isis, once you take out the wyrm and all, werewolves are basically furry talibans and routinely engage in acts that would bring most of the world antiterrorism organisations on their ass, Its just that the books don't dwell on it too much, they are also present in the cities in considerable numbers (glass walkers, bone gnawers and possibly other small camps of ronins) which makes sense since its where the wyrm is bigger and even living in rural areas doesn't mean much with the current information technology.<br /> <br /> Regarding the wyrm covering up their fuck ups, I'm pretty sure that they will wise up in the future and will bring more attention toward the garous, its just easier this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T07:35:53-07:00","id":1477211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477187#post1477187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you play werewolf heart of the forest?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. And I don't think the perspective of a single limited plot will change my view on the general aspects of the game. If with multiple choices you can't do different than butchering scores of humans, then this is a clear limitation on the game's premises. It is fun to think several RPG books on an RPG setting don't dwell on such relevant matter for the game, but a single Choose-Your-Path novel reveals the truth.<br /> <br /> Even within cities most werewolf activity is in out-of-the-way places, as their enemies don't want attention either, and I don't think the literal forces of capital C Corruption and Freak Legion-style Evil For Giggles will change their stance on attention just to pit unprepared hunters against the Garou (when those forces already have access to heavy duty military assets prepared to fight werewolves and enhanced by the Wyrm). All that before we talk about so many Rituals, Talens, Fetishes, Gifts and Totems that can help the Garou either not producing traces of their passages or erasing them afterwards.<br /> <br /> You can consider that their definitely unsubtle tactics draw a lot of attention and that is fine, what I'm saying is that it isn't necessarily an unavoidable, the-only-logical-conclusion approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T07:51:55-07:00","id":1477213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477211#post1477211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. And I don't think the perspective of a single limited plot will change my view on the general aspects of the game. If with multiple choices you can't do different than butchering scores of humans, then this is a clear limitation on the game's premises. It is fun to think several RPG books on an RPG setting don't dwell on such relevant matter for the game, but a single Choose-Your-Path novel reveals the truth.<br /> <br /> Even within cities most werewolf activity is in out-of-the-way places, as their enemies don't want attention either, and I don't think the literal forces of capital C Corruption and Freak Legion-style Evil For Giggles will change their stance on attention just to pit unprepared hunters against the Garou (when those forces already have access to heavy duty military assets prepared to fight werewolves and enhanced by the Wyrm). All that before we talk about so many Rituals, Talens, Fetishes, Gifts and Totems that can help the Garou either not producing traces of their passages or erasing them afterwards.<br /> <br /> You can consider that their definitely unsubtle tactics draw a lot of attention and that is fine, what I'm saying is that it isn't necessarily an unavoidable, the-only-logical-conclusion approach.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You misread my example, I mentioned the game because I think its a very good rapresentation of how a werewolf game can go and you can indeed finish the game with limited bloodshed (a lot of people are going to die regardless though) but the most straighforward method will always be violence and that is indeed a staple of the game, you are not going to convince me that people play werewolf with anything other in mind than killing things, that is just what the game is about and pretty much a front piece for most of the fiction in the books.<br /> <br /> Regarding cities, rituals etc. do you realize that vampires had all of that too? That didn't help them and they are arguably better at keeping things quiet than werewolves, what makes you think that giant monsters with a penchant for raging and murdering everything around them are going to fare any better than careful predators who are pretty much built to pass unnoticed among humans?<br /> <br /> I honestly think that its indeed the only possible conclusion based on the material released so far, maybe it won't be the SI specifically but I'm definitely sure that werewolves will have hunters hunting them down and I don't think it will necessarily be the wyrm behind them either, I guess we will have to wait for W5 and see how it goes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T08:31:58-07:00","id":1477215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477183#post1477183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know who should the S.I focus on? Kinfolk and Skin Dancers. [...]<br /> This way, the S.I can easily affect the garou without ever being just a bother in the battlefield.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sooner or later the S.I. will figure out that being a Garou is inherited. And then they will try to get access to DNA databases (not the D.N.A. werewolf antagonist group).<br /> <br /> All kinds of companies which store DNA data and either names of those whom the DNA belong to, or have documented characteristics to the DNA sample like hair-, skin- and eye-colour, or known inherited diseases. Companies for example store them for research purposes. To either steal those or appropriate them with a secret FISA-order? Totally possible for intelligence agencies.<br /> <br /> Once they have access they can analyse blood splatter from crime scenes and make pretty damn good predictions about who the blood belongs to or even find the name of your cousin thrice removed. From there they can make assumptions how far off they are in terms of generations they have to trace back. And sure, that might be hundreds of potential werewolves, but for an organisation with the computing power and man power the intelligence apparatus has at it's disposal, that can be managed. Also, they can usually determine gender, so halve of the potential garou are just removed from the suspect pool...<br /> And, either with FISA-order or not, the agencies could start to just covertly get more DNA samples of potential relatives of the suspect and add them to their databases, closing in on the garou's identity.<br /> <br /> Even in the real world we might not be so far away from this to work. It is just a matter of time until some organisation has a large enough database to make this work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T08:40:53-07:00","id":1477217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477215#post1477215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooner or later the S.I. will figure out that being a Garou is inherited. And then they will try to get access to DNA databases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. While S.I might not be a combat threat, they can easily kneecap a kinfolk community and sept supply lines.<br /> <br /> Granted, there is no 'werewolf-gene', but you can still do DNA tests on killed werewolves to trace lineages just as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T08:45:53-07:00","id":1477218,"title":"","content":"Once they start going after their families, they will have garous by the balls, especially the younger ones who aren't yet indoctrinated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T09:17:38-07:00","id":1477222,"title":"","content":"Well, it all depends on how good their Technocracy backing is.<br /> When Martin Ericsson first told his idea about the S.I. during a Convention in Germany back in the day, he suggested that this was a thing, but I'm not sure what made it to the books in the end.<br /> <br /> For, if they don't have that backing, the Glass Walkers will make use of technology spirits to mess with their databases and possibly let the S.I. chase their own tails (figuratively), or possibly send them after vampires to keep them busy while the Garou themselves deal with the real danger to Gaia. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T03:00:22-07:00","id":1477318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477213#post1477213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misread my example, I mentioned the game because I think its a very good rapresentation of how a werewolf game can go</div> </div> </div> </div>You gave your example directly declaring &quot;the books don't dwell on it too much&quot;, and your conclusion wasn't that a WtA game <b>can</b> go as that (which it certainly can), it was that most Werewolf activity <i>necessarily</i> go as that.<br /> <br /> So there was no misreading. It was exactly what you said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477213#post1477213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the most straighforward method will always be violence and that is indeed a staple of the game, you are not going to convince me that people play werewolf with anything other in mind than killing things, that is just what the game is about and pretty much a front piece for most of the fiction in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said otherwise.<br /> <br /> What's in question isn't if Garou are violent (they are), but how much frequently their activities necessarily leave a trail that can be followed to the point of the observer reaching the necessary conclusions to be aware of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477213#post1477213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding cities, rituals etc. do you realize that vampires had all of that too?</div> </div> </div> </div>About cities, not only is werewolf activity in them far rarer, despite two urban tribes, because most werewolves simply despise cities and don't care about them, you willfully ignore the point where those activities are limited in space to their own buildings and their infrequent targets (infrequent as, it apparently must be pointed out, Garou aren't literally on combat missions every day, thrice a day, those things aren't a constant despite preparedness having to be).<br /> <br /> Vampire are constantly vampires. They're <i>blankbodies</i> after all, their default state is a walking corpse no matter how good they are pretending to not be (and most aren't that good, people simply won't assume unless they're, you know, paranoid <i>hunters</i>). They're all over the place in cities as walking corpses, they infiltrate all social strata as walking corpses. Werewolves are for all purposes normal humans most of the time. There is no technological means of detection that can possibly identify a werewolf in Homid. Worse, they rarely infiltrate social infrastructure, and when they do so it isn't actually infiltration most of the time, it is literally that their families and friends are well positioned. Most kinfolk are legitimately where they are, they're not pretending anything, and even urban werewolves are frequently the same if they're not Caern-bound.<br /> <br /> On rituals the comparison is ludicrous. Among vampires rituals are a very niche thing and magic in general outside Disciplines is a fluke. But werewolves have so much access to it that evidence-cleaning magic (be it fetishes, talens or gifts) is standard procedure for most urban Septs, leaving home without it is almost as leaving naked. Gifts that mess with evidence or witnesses are level 1, fetishes too. Not to say that Garou can literally ask spirits for magical help just by Stepping Sideways and asking. It isn't guaranteed to work, but we're talking an action they all can attempt just by being the splat, no nothing required.<br /> <br /> Not to say that most times werewolves simply won't walk down the street in <i>Crinos</i>. Not only are they able to only change away from any witness that matters, you ignored all the times I mentioned the Umbra. It is completely outside direct human experience, there's no way for the SI to be able to pierce the Umbra without being specifically meant to by the authors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477213#post1477213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That didn't help them and they are arguably better at keeping things quiet than werewolves, what makes you think that giant monsters with a penchant for raging and murdering everything around them are going to fare any better than careful predators who are pretty much built to pass unnoticed among humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves don't fare better, they barely try to not be noticed <b>by their enemies</b>. The thing is, werewolves aren't generally dealing with human society, I'm talking about their ability to not leave traces for people they don't interact with, not to not be noticed by their targets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477213#post1477213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly think that its indeed the only possible conclusion based on the material released so far,</div> </div> </div> </div>So you think the only possible conclusion to link disparage terrorist attacks with little observable relation to one another and little to no evidence that can be traced back (not all of them have blood, either, as werewolves can clean it with easily accessible magic), perpetrated by what the best investigation will at most reveal to be attackers that appeared out of thin air then vanished, not to say when all evidence just points to wild animal attack, <i>the <b>ONLY</b></i> possible conclusion is that werewolves exist?<br /> <br /> It just seems to me like jumping a <u><b>lot</b></u> of conclusions only because you already know the answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1476953-should-the-s-i-fight-werewolves-more?p=1477213#post1477213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">maybe it won't be the SI specifically but I'm definitely sure that werewolves will have hunters hunting them down</div> </div> </div> </div>This whole conversation is about the SI, do not move goalposts. No one ever said there are no werewolf hunters. Or even that it isn't possible for the SI to know about them if the authors decide they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}